Z||000000||Alex2004||06-22-2001||11:29 PM||||Today i was messing w/ my car, and accidently pushed the "panic" button on my remote (does horn honk)  and it honked twice and then the horn got stuck and wouldn't go off so i pulled the horn relay out, we bought a new relay before b/c the horn's didn't work, and tought that would fix it, so i took that one out, and just barly put the old relay in and it still was honking, so i left it out and locked and unlocked my car w/ remote, and pushed the panic also, and it just flashed the lights thinking that maybe it was the alarm box messing it up, but it wasn't, check the horn wire under the dash to see if it was gounding somehow but it was connected, check the connections at the horn's and they were on tight, and the horn grounds are good too b/c i messed w/ them about a month ago.  Do any of you know what's wrong?  or what else i should check?<BR>Let me know, thanks...<P>Alex...   <A HREF="mailto:abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com">abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com</A>  ||||reg||8
Z||000001||PBJ||06-23-2001||11:11 AM||||unplug your alarm module and see if it stops because thats what you were pressing when it messed up.  Next I would remove horn pad and unplug wire from horn pad into center of steering wheel-twist in black or white plug with the red wire.  Hope this helps?????||||reg||1
